$Body = @"
## Purpose

Canonicalize current CaptivPortal testing ownership effective 2026-08-27.

## Final testing boundary

**Coder**
- runs focused/minimal automated tests only inside the current TASK/module scope;
- may create/change tests belonging to the implementation;
- may repeat those same targeted tests during development;
- does not execute unrelated-module, cross-module, broader or full repository regression.

If cross-module proof is required, Coder either requests Owner/Tech Lead/Central Lab execution or prepares the test without running it.

**Owner / Tech Lead / Central Lab**
- own cross-module and broader regression;
- own full pytest / full repository suite;
- own release and differential baseline/candidate gates;
- own official PASS/FAIL and acceptance.

## Central Lab physical ownership

- Tech Lead defines exact artifact, commands/gate procedure and acceptance criteria.
- Owner physically operates `C:\CaptivPortal-Lab` and launches the official regression.
- Owner + Tech Lead analyze evidence and issue PASS/FAIL/return-to-coder.
- Coder may patch the Lab directory only under an explicit prep-only instruction and stops before official execution.

## Scope

Documentation / governance only.

Changed files:

$($ExpectedPaths | ForEach-Object { "- ``$_``" } | Out-String)

No runtime code changes.
No test-code changes.
No production changes.
Historical FINAL TASK/reports are not rewritten.

Base: ``$Expected``
Commit: ``$Commit``

Created as Draft. Merge remains Owner-controlled.
"@

